{"title":"Career roadmap · News Anchor","role":"News Anchor","summary":"A News Anchor presents and contextualises news for television, digital video, radio or other broadcast platforms. The role combines journalism, research, interviewing, script writing, live presentation, fact-checking, voice delivery and editorial judgment.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Journalism & Mass Communication"},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Direct alignment, but News Anchor is usually not the first job. A common route is through reporting, desk work, production or digital journalism before moving into anchoring."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A BA in Journalism & Mass Communication is a directly relevant degree, but becoming a strong anchor requires substantial newsroom experience, on-camera practice and a demonstrable understanding of journalism ethics."}]},{"heading":"Typical route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA Journalism & Mass Communication","Journalism Internship","Reporter/News Desk/Production Assistant","Junior News Anchor/Correspondent","News Anchor","Senior Anchor","Prime-Time/Lead Anchor","Editorial/News Leadership"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build journalism fundamentals, reporting, writing, voice, camera presence and newsroom skills."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Gain newsroom experience and develop expertise in a specific beat such as politics, business, technology or international affairs."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress to Senior Anchor, Specialist Anchor or Lead Correspondent."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Move toward Editorial Lead, News Editor, Executive Producer, News Presenter or independent media leadership."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Journalism fundamentals + current affairs"},{"text":"Journalism courses + daily news"},{"text":"20 news summaries"},{"text":"Journalism foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"News writing + script writing"},{"text":"Newsroom examples"},{"text":"20 broadcast scripts"},{"text":"Writing"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Voice, diction + presentation"},{"text":"Voice/presentation training"},{"text":"10 recorded bulletins"},{"text":"Presentation"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Reporting + interviewing"},{"text":"Field assignments"},{"text":"5 field reports/interviews"},{"text":"Reporting"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Newsroom/broadcast internship"},{"text":"TV/digital newsroom"},{"text":"Internship + published work"},{"text":"Industry exposure"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Live presentation + specialised beat"},{"text":"News projects"},{"text":"10 professional demo videos"},{"text":"Employability"}],[{"text":"Honours Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Advanced broadcast journalism"},{"text":"Dissertation/media project"},{"text":"Investigative/feature project"},{"text":"Expertise"}],[{"text":"Honours Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Professional showreel"},{"text":"Mock/live broadcasts"},{"text":"2–3 minute anchor reel"},{"text":"Job readiness"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects to prioritise"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Journalism"},{"text":"Mass Communication"},{"text":"News Reporting"},{"text":"News Writing"},{"text":"Broadcast Journalism"},{"text":"Television Production"},{"text":"Radio Journalism"},{"text":"Digital Journalism"},{"text":"Media Ethics"},{"text":"Media Law"},{"text":"Political Communication"},{"text":"Public Affairs"},{"text":"Photojournalism"},{"text":"Video Production"},{"text":"Media Research"},{"text":"Current Affairs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical and professional skills"},{"type":"h","text":"Journalism"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"News gathering"},{"text":"Fact-checking"},{"text":"Source verification"},{"text":"Interviewing"},{"text":"News writing"},{"text":"Script writing"},{"text":"Headline writing"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Investigative journalism"},{"text":"Breaking-news workflow"},{"text":"Editorial judgment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"On-camera"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Voice modulation"},{"text":"Diction"},{"text":"Pronunciation"},{"text":"Teleprompter reading"},{"text":"Camera presence"},{"text":"Facial expression"},{"text":"Body language"},{"text":"Live improvisation"},{"text":"Interview technique"},{"text":"Crisis/live-event handling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Production"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Video editing"},{"text":"Audio editing"},{"text":"Lighting basics"},{"text":"Studio production"},{"text":"Teleprompter"},{"text":"Live broadcasting"},{"text":"OBS or similar tools"},{"text":"Premiere Pro/DaVinci Resolve"},{"text":"Canva"},{"text":"Basic graphics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital journalism"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"YouTube"},{"text":"Short-form video"},{"text":"Social journalism"},{"text":"Mobile journalism"},{"text":"SEO"},{"text":"Audience analytics"},{"text":"Digital storytelling"},{"text":"Multimedia reporting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI-era journalism"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted transcription"},{"text":"Research assistance"},{"text":"Fact-checking AI outputs"},{"text":"Deepfake awareness"},{"text":"Synthetic-media verification"},{"text":"Source authentication"},{"text":"Responsible AI use in journalism"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio target"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"20 professionally written news scripts"},{"text":"10 recorded news bulletins"},{"text":"5 field reports"},{"text":"5 interview videos"},{"text":"3 breaking-news simulations"},{"text":"3 long-form features"},{"text":"2 investigative/research projects"},{"text":"2 specialised news programmes"},{"text":"1 digital-news channel/project"},{"text":"Professional anchor showreel"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Your showreel is one of the most important pieces of evidence for an anchoring career."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Learn from","Senior role it leads to"],"rows":[[{"text":"General News"},{"text":"Reporting + presentation"},{"text":"Newsroom"},{"text":"Senior News Anchor"}],[{"text":"Political News"},{"text":"Politics + public affairs"},{"text":"Political reporting"},{"text":"Political Anchor"}],[{"text":"Business News"},{"text":"Economics + finance"},{"text":"Financial journalism"},{"text":"Business Anchor"}],[{"text":"Technology News"},{"text":"Technology + journalism"},{"text":"Tech reporting"},{"text":"Technology Anchor"}],[{"text":"International News"},{"text":"Geopolitics + languages"},{"text":"International affairs"},{"text":"International Affairs Anchor"}],[{"text":"Sports News"},{"text":"Sports + broadcasting"},{"text":"Sports journalism"},{"text":"Sports Anchor"}],[{"text":"Investigative Journalism"},{"text":"Research + verification"},{"text":"Investigative projects"},{"text":"Investigative Journalist"}],[{"text":"Digital News"},{"text":"Video + social + analytics"},{"text":"Digital newsroom"},{"text":"Digital News Lead"}],[{"text":"Regional-Language News"},{"text":"Language + journalism"},{"text":"Regional media"},{"text":"Regional News Anchor"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Evolve and stay relevant, 2035–2046"},{"type":"p","text":"Traditional television is only one part of modern news presentation. Future anchors will increasingly work across television, YouTube, podcasts, short-form video, livestreams and social platforms."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile will therefore combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Journalism","On-Camera Presentation","Research","Digital Video","Data Literacy","Verification","Domain Expertise"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"An anchor with genuine subject expertise—such as economics, technology, science, international affairs or public policy—can develop stronger long-term credibility than someone relying only on presentation skills."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Government/public broadcasting"},{"type":"table","header":["Organisation / route","Relevant exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"Prasar Bharati","url":"https://prasarbharati.gov.in/"},{"text":"Public broadcasting, TV/radio and news"}],[{"text":"Doordarshan","url":"https://prasarbharati.gov.in/"},{"text":"Television news and presentation"}],[{"text":"All India Radio","url":"https://prasarbharati.gov.in/"},{"text":"Radio journalism and news"}],[{"text":"University media centres"},{"text":"Student journalism and broadcasting"}],[{"text":"State public broadcasters/media units"},{"text":"Regional news and reporting"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Private media opportunities"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Television news channels"},{"text":"Digital news organisations"},{"text":"Newspapers"},{"text":"News websites"},{"text":"Radio networks"},{"text":"YouTube news teams"},{"text":"OTT/current-affairs platforms"},{"text":"Production houses"},{"text":"Regional-language media"},{"text":"Business/technology/sports media"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant organisations include Network18, Times Network, Zee and Sony Pictures Networks India, subject to current openings.","url":"https://www.nw18.com/"},{"type":"flow","items":["A newsroom internship","published/telecast work","a professional anchor showreel."],"sep":"+","label":"Best internship evidence"}]},{"heading":"Certifications in demand","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Certification/course","Cost","When","Why it helps"],"rows":[[{"text":"Journalism/News Reporting course"},{"text":"Free and paid options"},{"text":"Year 1–2"},{"text":"Journalism fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Br