","Business/Tech/Political/International Correspondent","Specialist Anchor"]},{"type":"p","text":"Leadership route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Anchor","Senior Anchor","Executive Producer","News Editor","Editorial Head"]},{"type":"h","text":"Domain specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Adding a strong subject area can significantly strengthen an anchor's profile:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Economics & business"},{"text":"Politics & public policy"},{"text":"Technology & AI"},{"text":"Science & health"},{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Sports"},{"text":"Environment & climate"},{"text":"Defence/geopolitics"},{"text":"Law"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046"},{"type":"p","text":"The future news presenter will increasingly be a multi-platform journalist, not just a television personality. Strong professionals will be able to research, verify, interview, present live, produce digital video, interpret data and communicate across TV, streaming, podcasts and social media."},{"type":"p","text":"The most durable profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Journalistic credibility","subject expertise","presentation ability","digital production","fact verification."],"sep":"+"}]}]}